room where introverts can recharge. It=E2=80=99s also had a =E2=80=9CValuab=
ly Quiet=E2=80=9D program since 2021 to help supervisors and colleagues und=
erstand introverts, from how they best get stuff done to how they show enth=
usiasm.

- Accounting firm KPMG has placed individual desks near grouped desks, allo=
wing introverts to listen and be near, but not directly in the mix.

- Other companies and organizations have been launching employee resource g=
roups (ERGs) that offer more introvert-friendly ways to socialize =E2=80=94=
 book clubs, crafts, online forums, etc.

- Biopharmaceutical company Sobi=E2=80=99s Quiet ERG (https://www.sobi.com/=
usa/en/dei?_hsenc=3Dp2ANqtz-_DudBNYeVyyIQalCe52IX3k7vLSfRxlErqfP2kukJlQJ9lv=
z56AZn4WK8muNOZoGoXge49mCZE65S470mz6z_qKaUYxw&_hsmi=3D396885155 ) allows in=
troverts to contribute ideas and perspectives in ways that work for them.

Fun fact: Beyond extroverts and introverts, there are ambiverts (they=E2=80=
=99re somewhere in the middle) and omniverts (https://www.simplypsychology.=
org/what-is-an-omnivert-meaning-and-traits.html?_hsenc=3Dp2ANqtz-_DudBNYeVy=
yIQalCe52IX3k7vLSfRxlErqfP2kukJlQJ9lvz56AZn4WK8muNOZoGoXge49mCZE65S470mz6z_=
qKaUYxw&_hsmi=3D396885155 ) (they flip between extremes, though there=E2=80=
=99s not much scientific research on this type). New is =E2=80=9Cotroverts =
(https://www.theguardian.com/society/2025/aug/20/are-you-an-otrovert-why-th=
is-personality-type-could-be-your-greatest-gift?_hsenc=3Dp2ANqtz-_DudBNYeVy=
yIQalCe52IX3k7vLSfRxlErqfP2kukJlQJ9lvz56AZn4WK8muNOZoGoXge49mCZE65S470mz6z_=
qKaUYxw&_hsmi=3D396885155 ) ,=E2=80=9D coined by psychiatrist Rami Kaminski=
 last year to describe people who feel perpetually on the outside.

=F0=9F=94=97 (https://thehustle.co/news/finally-some-peace-and-quiet-for-th=
