Increase in street- and vehicle-related crimes around Chicago neighborhoods=
 that offer e-scooter rentals, according to a recent study via (https://www=
.wsj.com/lifestyle/cars/e-scooter-rentals-crime-e88a9f07?mod=3Dbusiness_fea=
t4_autos_pos3&_hsenc=3Dp2ANqtz-_DudBNYeVyyIQalCe52IX3k7vLSfRxlErqfP2kukJlQJ=
9lvz56AZn4WK8muNOZoGoXge49mCZE65S470mz6z_qKaUYxw&_hsmi=3D396885155 ) The Wa=
ll Street Journal. Since the Midwestern city introduced electric scooters i=
n 2019, crime rates have risen in the areas where they=E2=80=99re available=
, leading researchers to conclude that the fast, easy-to-obtain, easy-to-di=
scard two-wheelers have become vehicles of choice among criminals like bag =
snatchers and car thieves.

It=E2=80=99s not hard to imagine such a scenario playing out, though Lime p=
robably wishes that wasn=E2=80=99t the case =E2=80=94 naturally, the e-scoo=
ter rental company, which services the Chicago area, rejected the study's f=
indings.

